add(H2("7.3 Real-world streams"));
add(P("Table 5 summarises the real streams. All methods except split CP stay within 0.008 of nominal coverage. The clearest effect appears on **MachineTemp**, the NAB stream containing documented system failures and operating-mode changes. Wrapping ACI reduces the mean width from 5.53 to 4.28 (−22.5%) at essentially unchanged coverage (0.900 vs. 0.898), cuts the fraction of infinite intervals from 0.75% to 0.04%, and lowers UCT from 17.5% to 14.5%. Wrapping QT reduces width by 9.5%, and wrapping DtACI by 4.1%, together with fewer infinite intervals (2.21% to 1.66%). Figure 5 shows that after each abnormal episode ACI remains inflated for a long time, whereas MARS(ACI) resets once scores return to their normal level. The cost is a lower worst-case rolling coverage (0.44 vs. 0.65): immediately after some resets, the small post-change buffer under-estimates the quantile of a still-evolving regime."));
